    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2939" root="بغض" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَغِيضٌ</span></b>  <i>Hateful; odious; and object of hatred:</i>
(S, A, Msb, * K:) <i>hated;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَغُوضٌ</span></b>  (TA)
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبْغَضٌ</span></b> : (Msb, * TA:) pl. of the first, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُغَضَآءُ</span>.
(A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Some say that it has also the contr.
signification of <i>Hating; i. q.</i> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُبْغِضٌ</span></b> : (TA:)
and Skr explains ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِغْضَةٌ</span></b>  as signifying people
<i>hating</i> thee. (L, TA. *)

